<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Mamluk War (1516–1517)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1517">1517</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> War was a conflict between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> in 1516–1517. Ottoman victories at Marj Dabiq in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and Ridaniya near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> brought Syria, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> under Ottoman rule in 1517. The war made the Ottoman Empire the leading power of the Islamic world.</p></div>
